<title>AUSTRALIA: Cultus shares dip after recovery rate talk.</title>
<headline>Cultus shares dip after recovery rate talk.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in oil and gas group Cultus Petroleum NL dipped 15 cents to A$3.75 on Monday after the company said it believed recovery rates at the Cornea oil field were likely to be better than those indicated by the joint venture operator, Shell Australia Ltd, the Australian unit of the Royal Dutch/Shell Group.</p>
<p>Shell told Reuters on Friday the recovery rate at the offshore Western Australia field could be as low as five percent, with a range of five to 35 percent a likely result.</p>
